Z||000025||The Fieromaster||08-20-2001||11:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B>Welcome, pull up a chair and stay a while.<BR>I too speak for the voices in my head which are not in any way related to Fieromasters<BR>voices but may be the same voices that your postman hears.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>DAVE you bad little monkey! Is that why my postman kept chanting "Must work on GT must work on GT"?  He scared the hell outta me!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Boomtastic||08-21-2001||01:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bazooka:<BR>*****************************************<BR>Boomtastic,<BR>     That photo of the gray Fiero with TPI and front engine looks a little dangerous. What's in it and how'de ya do it????<BR>MK[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Bazooka,<P>Well, first of all it's not trick photography or an Adobe enhanced image. It's an '86 coupe with a GT body, 2x3 tube chassis from front to back holding an '87 Chevy 383 (350 bored .030 over and a 400 crank). Transmission is a beefed up TH350. Rear end is a Ford 8" narrowed and hung in a 4 link suspension. The floor was raised up to compensate for the tube chassis, and the front firewall (from where the foot rests in the carpet are) forward was removed to make room for the engine. The gas tank was taken out and switched to a fuel cell, which now rests over the center of the axle. The battery is also over the axle, towards the rear of the car. This puts weight over the rear end, keeping it down during take off. With the gas tank out, the center "tunnel" was expanded to accept the bell housing of the transmission. All the body panels still hang on the original mounting points, so body lines are kept straight. The strut towers were cut and grafted into the wheel tubs to keep things aligned. The car currently rides on Weld rims - 10" in the rear, 3½ fronts. Slicks - 27x10 Goodyear Eagles - are on the rear, but will be replaced by 295/50R15 street tires shortly. (Yes, this WILL be street driven and legal!)<P>Hopefully that will help to build a mental picture until I can get things working back here. My ISP shut down port 80 due to the Code Red worm, which effectively shut down my web server.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> If not, let me know, or email me and I'll send you some pics.<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Bazooka||08-21-2001||07:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally Hopefully that will help to build a mental picture until I can get things working back here. My ISP shut down port 80 due to the Code Red worm, which effectively shut down my web server.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> If not, let me know, or email me and I'll send you some pics.<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>*****************************************<BR>Bommtastic,   That sounds like a great setup. Hope to see some pics in the future. Is the weight similar to a regular GT? I know that various V8 Fieros (like my own) Do encounter problems with Transes, Harnessing Power, Suspension, Cooling system Problems and Access problems. It sounds like you may have bypassed a lot of these problems by designing your Fiero as you did. And street legal, wow! You may need wheelie bars to keep it on the road. Nice! <BR>||||reg||1
